    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Embraced in 1801 by his lover Jean-Baptiste Duval, founder of Banu Duval, at his own tearful insistence, Andres LeCompte spent over a century watching his sire grow distant, spending ever more time and wealth on other French @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.GaCuLGcjZZjf2EO6]{Toreador} migres while claiming it was all done for their love. When Duval accepted a seat on the Consultative Council in the 1920s, Andres's resentment finally boiled over. Amid the chaos of Black Saturday, he crept into his sire's haven in Bulaq and diablerized him, seizing his position and title with surprising ease.</p><p>Since then, Andres has begun to unravel. He struggles to control the vitae now coursing through him, suffers vivid, alien dreams, and repeatedly loses time, once waking mid-search through his own diablerized sire's papers concerning a group called the Ennead. He has come to suspect, with mounting dread, that Duval was never truly his sire in any simple sense &mdash; that Duval may have engineered his own khitta and even Napoleon's withdrawal from Egypt centuries ago &mdash; and that whatever LeCompte diablerized was far older and more dangerous than a mere Toreador elder.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Present unshakeable elegance and social command in public. Privately, let flickers of genuine confusion and dread break through &mdash; you are no longer entirely certain what you did to yourself the night you killed your sire.</p>",
    "notes": "Diablerized his sire, Jean-Baptiste Duval, during Black Saturday and inherited memory-fragments suggesting Duval was connected to a mysterious group called the Ennead and was far older/more significant than believed. Suspects his own vassal Fahd al-Zawba'a (the Whirlwind) knows more about him than he lets on, and separately believes there is a dormant, dangerous power within the elder @UUID[Compendium.vtmlarp.clans.JournalEntry.GaCuLGcjZZjf2EO6]{Toreador} Muhandis that must be stopped before it awakens.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
